# Window chrome is off-limits

Dosa uses `.windowStyle(.hiddenTitleBar)` on the `WindowGroup` in `DosaApp.swift`. That is the
**only** window-styling call in the codebase. Traffic lights overlay the sidebar's top-left, which
is why `SidebarView`'s icon row has `.padding(.top, 34)`.

`Scripts/check-window-chrome.sh` runs at the start of `./build.sh` and fails the build on
everything below. If it fires, delete the offending call — do not loosen the check.

## Never

```swift
.toolbar(.hidden, for: .windowToolbar)        // kills the sidebar toggle + traffic lights
.toolbar(removing: .sidebarToggle)            // leaves no way to reopen a collapsed sidebar
.toolbar(removing: .title)                    // same class of chrome collapse
NavigationSplitView(columnVisibility: $x)     // let the split view own its visibility
window.standardWindowButton(.zoomButton)      // wrong coordinate space; see below
window.styleMask / .titleVisibility / .titlebarAppearsTransparent   // fights SwiftUI
```

Do not add a `ToolbarItem` sidebar toggle or an overlay button to "reposition" the system one.
The traffic lights live in the window's titlebar view, a **sibling** of SwiftUI's content view, so
any hand-placed button is measured in the wrong space and drifts with window size, sidebar width,
and macOS version. The last attempt put the toggle in the vertical middle of the sidebar.

The system toggle sitting near the split rather than beside the traffic lights is standard macOS
placement (Notes, Mail). It is not a bug.

## Instead

For edge-to-edge content in the detail pane, the sanctioned pair (already in `ContentView`):

```swift
.toolbarBackground(.hidden, for: .windowToolbar)   // hides the material, keeps the toolbar
.background(Theme.current.editorBackgroundColor.ignoresSafeArea(edges: .top))
```

If a view sits too high or too low, adjust **that view's** padding and keep it in normal layout
flow. A top-anchored `VStack` or `.overlay(alignment: .top)` reaching into the titlebar region is
how the Welcome greeting ended up jammed against the window edge.

## Verify

Any UI-touching change: `./build.sh`, quit the running app, `open build/Dosa.app`, then confirm
traffic lights top-left, exactly one sidebar toggle, sidebar full-height with no dead strip above
its header, and Welcome + editor correct in light and dark. Full invariant list: §9b of
`docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md`.
